---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import CategoryChip from '../components/CategoryChip.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import NewsletterBlock from '../components/NewsletterBlock.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import portrait from '../assets/about/will.jpg';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const description =
	'Field notes from Will, Head of Marketing & Customer Experience at a UK education business, on building, marketing, and using AI in practice.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About · ${SITE_TITLE}`} description={description} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header current="about" />
		<main>
			<header class="hero">
				<figure class="polaroid taped">
					<Image src={portrait} alt="Will, smiling, on a cobbled harbourside" width={400} height={400} loading="eager" />
					<figcaption class="hand">Hello, I'm Will</figcaption>
				</figure>
				<h1>About</h1>
				<div class="byline">
					<strong>Will</strong>
					<span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
					<span>Head of Marketing &amp; CX</span>
					<span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
					<span>UK</span>
				</div>
				<p class="dek">{description}</p>
			</header>

			<section class="prose intro">
				<p>
					I'm Will, Head of Marketing &amp; Customer Experience at a UK education business,
					where I look after a marketing team, a lead generation function, and a customer
					solutions team.
				</p>
				<p>
					Most of what I do day-to-day sits at the intersection of three things: building
					an integrated acquisition and retention model, figuring out how AI actually
					changes marketing (rather than how it's supposed to), and helping my team do their
					best work.
				</p>
				<p>This site is where I write about what I'm learning in the open.</p>
			</section>

			<h2>What you'll find here</h2>
			<p class="prose lead">
				Field Notes is a working notebook, not a thought-leadership outlet. Posts tend to
				fall into three categories:
			</p>

			<div class="categories">
				<div class="cat-block">
					<div class="cat-left">
						<CategoryChip tag="building" size="lg" />
						<a class="fn-link browse" href={`${base}/blog/`}>Browse →</a>
					</div>
					<div class="cat-right">
						<p class="cat-title">Things I'm building</p>
						<p class="cat-body">
							AI tools, work systems, websites and side projects. I show the work: what I
							tried, what broke, and what I'd do differently. Most recently, a team of AI
							helpers for my marketing team, reports that write themselves, 3D demos for
							local businesses, and the site you're reading now.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="cat-block">
					<div class="cat-left">
						<CategoryChip tag="marketing" size="lg" />
						<a class="fn-link browse" href={`${base}/blog/`}>Browse →</a>
					</div>
					<div class="cat-right">
						<p class="cat-title">Marketing thinking</p>
						<p class="cat-body">
							How I'm approaching the work: campaigns, team structure, customer experience,
							the retention/acquisition handoff, the awkward bits no one writes about. Less
							framework-shopping, more "here's what we tried and what happened."
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="cat-block">
					<div class="cat-left">
						<CategoryChip tag="ai" size="lg" />
						<a class="fn-link browse" href={`${base}/blog/`}>Browse →</a>
					</div>
					<div class="cat-right">
						<p class="cat-title">AI, practically</p>
						<p class="cat-body">
							Where it earns its keep in real organisations, where it doesn't, and the gap
							between the demos and the day job. Written for colleagues and peers who are
							bored of the hype and want to know what's actually useful on a Tuesday
							morning.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<h2>Who I'm writing for</h2>
			<p class="prose">
				People doing the work, not watching it. Marketers, team leads, small business owners,
				anyone wondering what AI could actually do for them. You don't need to be technical.
				I'm not a developer either, so everything here is written in plain English. If I use
				a technical word, I'll explain it.
			</p>

			<h2>How I work</h2>
			<p class="prose">
				This isn't a course and it isn't a sales pitch. I'm a practitioner figuring it out
				in public, which means I'll be wrong sometimes, and I'd rather be wrong out loud
				than vague in private. If you'd like a hand getting started with AI, or just want
				to compare notes, I'm always happy to hear from people on LinkedIn.
			</p>
			<p class="prose">
				I write about Claude because it's the tool I use most, and the habits carry over to any
				AI assistant. I'm not paid by Anthropic, and nobody tells me what to write.
			</p>

			<h2>A note on work projects</h2>
			<p class="prose">
				Some of what I write about I built for my day job. I keep those anonymous: no company
				names, no colleagues, no customers and no real figures. The ideas and the lessons are
				real. The details that belong to other people stay out.
			</p>

			<NewsletterBlock />
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
<style>
	.hero {
		margin-bottom: 44px;
	}
	.hero::after {
		content: '';
		display: block;
		clear: both;
	}
	.polaroid {
		float: right;
		width: 220px;
		margin: 6px 0 20px 32px;
		padding: 12px 12px 6px;
		background: #fff;
		box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08), 0 10px 24px -12px rgba(40, 30, 10, 0.35);
		transform: rotate(2.5deg);
	}
	.polaroid img {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		aspect-ratio: 1;
		object-fit: cover;
	}
	.polaroid figcaption {
		text-align: center;
		font-size: 24px;
		color: var(--ink);
		padding: 8px 0 2px;
	}
	.hero h1 {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-weight: 500;
		font-size: 92px;
		margin: 0;
		line-height: 0.98;
		letter-spacing: -0.025em;
	}
	.byline {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 10px;
		margin-top: 24px;
		font-size: 14px;
		color: rgb(var(--text-muted));
		padding-bottom: 22px;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-soft);
	}
	.byline strong {
		color: rgb(var(--text));
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	.byline .sep {
		opacity: 0.4;
	}
	.dek {
		font-style: italic;
		color: rgb(var(--text-muted));
		font-size: 22px;
		line-height: 1.45;
		margin: 28px 0 0;
		max-width: 620px;
	}
	.intro {
		max-width: 680px;
	}
	main h2 {
		font-family: var(--font-atkinson);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 13px;
		line-height: 1;
		margin: 52px 0 18px;
		letter-spacing: 0.18em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: rgb(var(--text-muted));
	}
	.prose.lead {
		max-width: 680px;
	}
	.categories {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 20px;
		margin: 20px 0 24px;
	}
	.cat-block {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 180px 1fr;
		gap: 24px;
		padding: 20px 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-soft);
	}
	.cat-left {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: flex-start;
		gap: 10px;
	}
	.browse {
		font-size: 13px;
	}
	.cat-title {
		font-family: var(--font-atkinson);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 19px;
		color: rgb(var(--text));
		margin: 0 0 8px;
		line-height: 1.25;
		letter-spacing: -0.005em;
	}
	.cat-body {
		color: rgb(var(--text-muted));
		font-size: 17px;
		margin: 0;
		line-height: 1.55;
		max-width: 560px;
	}
	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.hero {
			margin-bottom: 32px;
		}
		.polaroid {
			width: 138px;
			margin: 0 0 14px 18px;
			padding: 8px 8px 4px;
		}
		.polaroid figcaption {
			font-size: 18px;
			padding-top: 4px;
		}
		.byline {
			clear: both;
			padding-top: 4px;
		}
		.hero h1 {
			font-size: 54px;
		}
		.dek {
			font-size: 19px;
			margin-top: 22px;
		}
		main h2 {
			font-size: 12px;
			margin: 36px 0 14px;
		}
		.categories {
			gap: 16px;
			margin: 16px 0;
		}
		.cat-block {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 10px;
			padding: 16px 0;
		}
		.cat-title {
			font-size: 17px;
		}
		.cat-body {
			font-size: 16px;
		}
	}
</style>
